.Dd August 27, 2026
.Dt C4AR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm c4ar
.Nd create C4 static libraries
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl +h
.Op Fl j Ar n
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl T Ar triplet
.Ar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Creates an archive (static library) from the given object files. This will be
compatible with the system
.Xr ar 1
utility, but contains additional metadata which the C4 tools, such as
.Xr c4ld 1 ,
or
.Xr c4if 1
can utilize.

The conventional archive filename is
.Pa *.c4a
to indicate that this archive file has the additional metadata, but nothing
enforces this.

The
.Nm
program also accepts the following flags:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl +
Embed metadata marking that this library will need C++ linkage. This is useful
if the library itself calls into C++, so when building the executable the
.Xr c4ld 1
linker will need to resolve and link the C++ libraries of the system as well.
.It Fl h
Print short help text and exit 100.
.It Fl j Ar n
Set the amount of worker threads to run for processing the object files to
.Ar n .
.It Fl o Ar file
Generate output into
.Ar file .
If not given, the default is
.Pa lib.c4a .

The process of creating archives from C4 objects is really similar to creating
normal C or C++ based archives. The difference is a bit of metadata that is
managed.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
On success,
.Nm
exits 0. In case of failure, the following are used:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 100
Invalid invocation. Flags or arguments malformed or missing.
.It 101
Unexpected error. Please file a bug report.
.It 111
General runtime error: syscall failure or LLVM error.
.El
